{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.BorelSingularity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.BorelSingularity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.BorelResummation"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.BorelSingularity.borel_singularity_lower_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.BorelSingularity.borel_singularity_lower_bound","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelSingularity.lean#L72-L86","doc":"**Borel singularity = A-polynomial period (conditional).**\nFor ANY Gevrey-1 sequence with growth constant `A > 0`:\nthe Borel transform converges on the disc of radius `1/A`,\nso the nearest singularity is at distance ≥ `1/A`.\n\nFor 4₁: plugging in `A = 1/V(4₁)` gives singularity at\ndistance ≥ V(4₁) = the period. The hypothesis that the\nperturbative coefficients ARE Gevrey-1(C, 1/V) is the\nsaddle-point analysis gap. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.BorelSingularity.borel_disc_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.BorelSingularity.borel_disc_bound","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelSingularity.lean#L53-L58","doc":"**Per-coefficient bound (restated).** Under Gevrey-1(C,A),\n`|borelCoeff a n · tⁿ| ≤ C · (A·|t|)ⁿ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.BorelSingularity.borel_convergence_radius_lower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.BorelSingularity.borel_convergence_radius_lower","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelSingularity.lean#L43-L51","doc":"**Inverse growth rate ≤ convergence radius.** If `0 < A` and\n`Gevrey1 a C A`, then `B(t)` converges for `|t| < 1/A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.BorelSingularity.borel_convergence_disc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.BorelSingularity.borel_convergence_disc","kind":"theorem","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BorelSingularity.lean#L34-L41","doc":"**The Borel convergence disc.** A Gevrey-1(C,A) sequence has Borel\ncoefficients bounded by `C · Aⁿ`, so the Borel transform converges\nabsolutely on the disc `{t : A·|t| < 1}`, i.e. radius ≥ 1/A. ","signatureChunk":0}]}